    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (81.27) pacing the squad as our premier offensive anchor. Facing Merrill Kelly, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a pitcher with an elevated 5.13 xERA, allowing his base projection to inflate significantly. He is flanked by **Andy Pages** (73.64), who similarly exploits this favorable matchup in the #2 hole, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.22), whose 14% boost from dynamic platoon modeling against right-hander Alek Manoah makes him a core play today. The strategic emphasis on speed remains paramount, and we expect **Gunnar Henderson** (63.19) and **Nasim Nunez** (63.69) to aggressively hunt bases despite facing sturdy arms like Nathan Eovaldi and the high-whiff potential of the opposing staff. \n\nThe primary lineup construction decision centered on the middle infield and outfield depth, with **Liam Hicks** (39.67) narrowly missing the cut. Despite his potential, the combination of Logan Gilbert\u2019s elite skill set and the strict 40-point efficiency floor mandated by our current bench management strategy relegated **Liam Hicks** to the pine. We are also monitoring the 40% rain risk hovering over the contest involving **Jorge Polanco** (49.78); while his score remains serviceable, any delay could dampen his output in a contest against Mlodzinski. Meanwhile, we remain without the services of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who are both sidelined, forcing us to lean heavily on the consistency of **Jackson Merrill** (68.30), whose robust platoon profile helps insulate our batting average category against Ronel Blanco. With **Drake Baldwin**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Jacob Wilson** rounding out the bottom third of the lineup, the focus remains on high-contact scenarios to navigate the varied xERA profiles we face across the diamond today.",
